  "visualBrief": "Individual Lucca Cathedral: asymmetric Romanesque marble west front with two large and one smaller deep portico arches, three arcaded tiers including a narrower upper gallery; long tiled nave/clerestory and lean-to aisles, cross transept, projecting chapels and rounded eastern apse. Tall southwest tan-brick/pale-marble campanile with graduated single/pair/triple/quadruple belfry arches and crenellations. Recessed portals, circular clerestory windows, blind side arcade ribs, cornices and sparse geometric stone inlays. Five existing shared ashlar/limestone/tile/brick/wood graphs, linear tints, metric UVs, flat normals and four budgeted browser levels. Current whole/component footprints and standard DEM. Exact marble carving/statues/inscriptions/mosaic, interior rooms, hidden roof joints and surveyed plaza/thresholds are approximate or excluded.",
