    "architecturalHeights": "Retained exact-QID OSM way180366824/Q1282278 matches current main35184552455656. All22 raw main vertices and11 component plans/tags remain exact after rigid rotation with no rescale. Current mapped campanile35185841751561 has69m height; other height/min_height tags are absent. The western portico, southwest tower, long eastward nave/cross transept and east rounded apse sign the retained axis. Nave/transept roof partitions are picture estimates within the mapped envelope. Approximate levels: portico14.5m, full-width marble galleries15..21.5m and22..28m, narrower central gallery28.5..35m; nave/transept eaves30m/ridges36m; aisle walls19.8m/lean-to joins26.5m; eastern side chapels22m/hips26m; projecting north/south side chapels13m/hips17m; apse30m/faceted roof35.8m. Campanile brick lower shaft0..47m, pale upper47..67m, open belfry tiers with one/two/three/four arches, crenellations67..69m. Recessed tier galleries, arch/column rhythm, clerestory circles, side blind arcades, portals and trim are picture approximations. No survey or engineering accuracy claimed."
